---
import ReferenceFigure from "./ReferenceFigure.astro";

const root = "/studies/plasma-projector-fitting-2026-11-17";
---

<div class="tactical-references">
  <ReferenceFigure>
    <a
      slot="image"
      href={`${root}/024-titanfall-mastiff.jpg`}
      aria-label="Enlarge Titanfall 2 Mastiff reference"
    >
      <img
        src={`${root}/024-titanfall-mastiff.jpg`}
        width="1920"
        height="1224"
        alt="Titanfall 2 Mastiff: a long continuous top line, compact receiver and narrow barrel projecting beyond its angular forebody"
      >
    </a>
    <h3>Titanfall 2 / The shotgun still points</h3>
    <p>
      The Mastiff's receiver, forebody and projecting muzzle follow one long
      axis. Changes in section and the forward projection give it direction. Its
      angular covers and repeated hardware sit along that line.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Take forward:</strong>
      a compact gun can preserve this directional hierarchy. The useful
      reference is the relationship between receiver and forward assembly; our
      fitting's shotgun proportions remain to be drawn. This is a gun-form
      reference, not a plasma reference.
    </p>
    <p class="credit">
      <a href="https://brockhaurd.artstation.com/projects/l5zGV"
        >Ryan Lastimosa — Mastiff Combat Shotgun</a
      >, Titanfall 2 / Respawn. Original production artwork, unaltered.
    </p>
  </ReferenceFigure>
  <ReferenceFigure>
    <a
      slot="image"
      href={`${root}/024-star-citizen-plasma-rifle.jpg`}
      aria-label="Enlarge Star Citizen plasma rifle concept reference"
    >
      <img
        src={`${root}/024-star-citizen-plasma-rifle.jpg`}
        width="2553"
        height="1911"
        alt="Kastak Arms plasma rifle concept: an elongated gun with an angular receiver, illuminated forward inset and repeated components below the forward firing axis"
      >
    </a>
    <h3>Star Citizen / Plasma within a gun</h3>
    <p>
      The Kastak Arms concept places a luminous inset and repeated working parts
      along a forward assembly. The receiver and muzzle remain distinct within
      an elongated rifle silhouette. Energy features are integrated into that
      structure.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Take forward:</strong>
      give plasma a visible location inside the projecting head. The casing can
      open around it while the gun keeps its lengthwise character. This is the
      historical Berserker concept associated with the Karna, not a claim about
      current production artwork.
    </p>
    <p class="credit">
      Cloud Imperium Games,
      <a href="https://starcitizen.tools/File:Berserker_4.jpg"
        >original concept sheet preserved by Star Citizen Wiki</a
      >. The archive identifies CIG's
      <a
        href="https://robertsspaceindustries.com/comm-link/engineering/15627-Kastak-Arms-Plasma-Rifle"
        >Kastak Arms Plasma Rifle presentation</a
      >
      as its source. Image unaltered.
    </p>
  </ReferenceFigure>
  <ReferenceFigure>
    <a
      slot="image"
      href={`${root}/024-district-9-assault-rifle.jpg`}
      aria-label="Enlarge District 9 assault rifle concept reference"
    >
      <img
        src={`${root}/024-district-9-assault-rifle.jpg`}
        width="2500"
        height="1767"
        alt="District 9 alien assault rifle: a long shallow white and orange body, a row of angled canisters along its top edge and a distinct dark forward end"
      >
    </a>
    <h3>District 9 / Machinery follows the line</h3>
    <p>
      The repeated canisters run along a shallow, elongated body. Large pale and
      orange surfaces preserve a clean overall read; the angled modules add
      unfamiliar technology without breaking the main firing direction.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Take forward:</strong>
      a small number of repeated parts can reinforce length and suggest a
      working system. The side-view composition is useful; its grip, stock,
      exact palette and full rifle length are not a fitting prescription. This
      is a sci-fi construction reference, not evidence of plasma mechanics.
    </p>
    <p class="credit">
      <a href="https://www.gregbroadmore.com/portfolio/district-9"
        >Greg Broadmore — District 9 alien assault rifle concept</a
      >, Wētā Workshop. Original artwork, unaltered.
    </p>
  </ReferenceFigure>
</div>
